et accessories, wall protection) and MEP equipment. Backing/blocking is often under-quantified.\n- Cabinet shop drawings will need dental equipment coordination (chairs, delivery systems, compressor, vacuum lines).\n\n---\n\n### 3. FINISHES (18 items)\n**Spec Sections:**\n- 092216 — Non-Structural Metal Framing (pages 133–140)\n- 092900 — Gypsum Board (pages 140–146)\n- 093013 — Ceramic Tiling (pages 146–153)\n- 095123 — Acoustical Tile Ceilings (pages 153–156)\n- 096513 — Resilient Base and Accessories (pages 156–159)\n- 096516 — Resilient Sheet Flooring (pages 159–163)\n- 097200 — Wall Coverings (pages 163–166)\n- 099123 — Interior Painting (pages 166–171)\n\n#### Metal Framing & GWB\n**Manufacturers:** CertainTeed/Saint-Gobain, Georgia-Pacific, National Gypsum, USG Corporation\n- Multiple GWB types specified (likely standard, moisture-resistant, abuse-resistant for healthcare)\n- VOC content limit: adhesives ≤50 g/L\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Hospital environment = likely abuse-resistant GWB (e.g., DensArmor, Fiberock) at high-traffic areas\n- Lead-lined GWB possible for dental X-ray rooms — **check drawings for X-ray equipment locations**\n- Partition types need careful reading from drawings — shared objects with two faces per BluePrint rules\n\n#### Ceramic Tiling (093013)\n**Manufacturers:** Laticrete, MAPEI (setting materials); Schluter Systems (edge trim/waterproofing)\n- **\"No substitutions allowed for finish tile materials\"** — tile selection is locked per drawings\n- Marble thresholds: ASTM C503, honed finish, abrasion-resistant\n- Mortar bed option specified — could indicate thick-set tile in some locations\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- No-substitution clause on tile — pricing must match specified product exactly\n- Marble thresholds at every tile-to-other-flooring transition — count from plans\n- Schluter waterproofing at wet areas (likely restrooms)\n\n#### ACT Ceilings (095123)\n**Manufacturers:** Armstrong World Industries (as indicated on drawings), Armstrong Ceiling & Wall Solutions\n- Product specific to drawings — need to cross-reference ceiling plans for types/patterns\n\n#### Resilient Flooring\n- **Base (096513):** Johnsonite (Tarkett) — rubber or vinyl base\n- **Sheet Flooring (096516):** Healthcare-grade resilient sheet. Heat-welded seams. Water-resistant adhesive.\n  - Sheet flooring in dental clinic = infection control surface\n  - Flash-cove base likely required at walls\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Heat-welded seams require skilled installer\n- Flash-coving = additional material and labor vs. straight base\n- Substrate prep critical — moisture testing, leveling, coating removal all specified\n\n#### Wall Coverings (097200)\n- Likely vinyl wall covering for healthcare durability\n- Check drawings for locations and types\n\n#### Interior Painting (099123)\n**Manufacturer:** Benjamin Moore & Co. (sole specified, multiple product lines)\n- Multiple paint systems for different substrates (GWB, metal, wood, CMU)\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Benjamin Moore sole-source — verify if \"or equal\" language exists\n- Distinguish ceiling paint from wall paint — dental suites may have varying ceiling heights\n- Check for high-bay or mechanical space ceiling conditions requiring different access/application\n- Hospital VOC requirements likely stricter than standard\n\n---\n\n### 4. SPECIALTIES (13 items)\n**Spec Sections:**\n- 102600 — Wall and Door Protection (pages 171–174)\n- 102800 — Toilet, Bath, and Laundry Accessories (pages 174–178)\n- 104416 — Fire Extinguishers (pages 178–180)\n\n#### Wall & Door Protection (102600)\n**Manufacturers:** Koroseal/Acrovyn; Altro Whitrock\n- Polycarbonate sheet wall protection: ASTM D6098, impact-resistant (15 ft-lbf min)\n- **Altro Whitrock** = PVC hygienic wall sheet — likely for dental operatory and/or sterilization areas\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Altro Whitrock is a specialty product — confirm if this is in addition to or in lieu of tile at wet walls\n- Koroseal corner guards, handrails, wall guards — healthcare standard but count-dependent\n- Blocking required behind all wall protection items — coordinate with rough carpentry\n\n#### Toilet Accessories (102800)\n**Basis of Design:** Bobrick (Bradley Corporation as alternate)\n- Full accessory package: mirrors, dispensers, grab bars, hooks, shelves, baby changing stations\n- GAMCO (Bobrick division) also listed for some items\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- ADA compliance on all accessory mounting heights\n- Grab bars require solid blocking — coordinate with framing\n- Baby changing stations noted in cut sheets — confirm locations\n\n#### Fire Extinguishers (104416)\n- Semi-recessed or surface-mounted cabinets\n- Coordinate with fire protection sub\n\n---\n\n### 5. OPENINGS / DOORS (6 items)\n**Spec Sections:**\n- 081113 — Hollow Metal Doors and Frames (pages 98–104)\n- 083113 — Access Doors and Frames (page 104)\n- 087100 — Door Hardware (pages 107–125)\n- 089119 — Fixed Louvers (page 125)\n\n**Manufacturers:**\n- Doors/Frames: Ceco Door (ASSA ABLOY), Curries (ASSA ABLOY)\n- Hardware: BEST (dormakaba), Sargent, dormakaba, Trimco\n- **Keying: Sargent to suit existing key system** — must match hospital's existing system\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- **18 pages of door hardware specs** — this is a detailed hardware schedule. Likely specified by a hardware consultant.\n- Keying must integrate with existing hospital master key system (Sargent)\n- Fire-rated doors/frames per NFPA 80 — coordination with fire-rated partition types\n- Access doors for MEP — coordinate locations with mechanical/electrical subs\n- Fixed louvers at mechanical spaces\n\n---\n\n### 6. THERMAL & MOISTURE PROTECTION (4 items)\n**Spec Sections:**\n- 078413 — Penetration Firestopping (pages 90–93)\n- 079200 — Joint Sealants (pages 93–98)\n\n**Key Products:**\n- Multiple sealant types specified (basis-of-design products)\n- Firestopping at all rated penetrations — UL listed systems\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Firestopping scope depends on quantity of rated walls — cross-reference with partition schedule\n- Hospital = lots of rated walls = significant firestopping scope\n- Joint sealants at multiple conditions — interior and potentially exterior\n\n---\n\n### 7. METALS (5 items)\n**Spec Section:** 055000 — Metal Fabrications\n- Miscellaneous steel items (lintels, supports, brackets)\n\n---\n\n### 8. FURNISHINGS (2 items)\n**Spec Sections:**\n- 122413 — Roller Window Shades (pages 180–186)\n- 123661.16 — Solid Surfacing Countertops (pages 186–192)\n\n**Key Products:**\n- **Countertops:** Corian (DuPont/now Corian Design) — solid surface\n- Roller shades: motorized or manual per drawings\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Corian countertops at dental operatories — likely specific edge profiles and integrated sinks\n- Verify if countertops are owner-furnished or contractor-furnished/installed\n- Roller shades — check if any are at interior borrowed-light windows vs. exterior\n\n---\n\n### 9. CONCRETE / MASONRY (2 items)\n- Concrete: 1 item (likely slab patching/infill at demo areas)\n- Masonry: 1 item (likely CMU infill at partition relocations)\n\n**🚩 FLAGS:**\n- Both are small quantities but require coordination with structural\n- Concrete curing in occupied hospital environment — dust/moisture control\n\n---\n\n## DRAWING SETS\n\n| Part | Pages | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| Part 1 | Small | Cover/general info |\n| Part 2 | Large (19MB) | Likely existing conditions / demo plans |\n| Part 3 | 30 sheets | Main architectural set |\n| Part 4 | 26 sheets | Likely MEP set |\n| Part 5 | 24 sheets | Likely MEP/electrical set |\n| Part 6 | ~9MB | Additional MEP or details |\n| Part 7 | ~8.5MB | Additional details/schedules |\n\nSheet index extracted for Parts 3-5 (80 sheets) — see sheet_index.json.\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL FLAGS SUMMARY\n\n### 🔴 HIGH PRIORITY\n0. **Henry Schein Dental Equipment Coordination** — Drawing Parts 5 show \"DENTAL MECHANICAL EQUIPMENT PLACEMENT TO BE COORDINATED WITH OWNER, CONTRACTOR AND HENRY SCHEIN EQUIPMENT SPECIALIST.\" This is owner-furnished specialty equipment requiring sub-floor conduit, dental air lines, water lines. GC must coordinate rough-in locations precisely with Henry Schein before framing/concrete work.\n1. **Occupied Hospital / ICRA Requirements** — All work in active healthcare facility. Infection control barriers, negative air, HEPA filtration mandatory. Work hours 7AM–3PM only.\n2. **Hazmat/ACM Abatement** — Item 7, lump sum. Old hospital building — likely ACM in floors, ceilings, pipe insulation. Scope undefined = pricing risk.\n3. **4th Floor Ceiling R&R** — Work on floor below requires access coordination with active hospital operations. 10% replacement allowance.\n4. **No Tile Substitutions** — Finish tile materials locked. Must price exactly what's specified.\n5. **Sargent Keying to Match Existing** — All locksets must integrate with hospital's existing Sargent master key system.\n\n### 🟡 MEDIUM PRIORITY\n6. **Lead-Lined GWB** — Dental X-ray rooms likely require radiation shielding. Check drawings for lead-lined partition requirements.\n7. **Altro Whitrock Hygienic Wall Panels** — Specialty product, limited installers. Clarify scope vs. ceramic tile.\n8. **Benjamin Moore Sole Source** — Verify substitution language for painting.\n9. **Corian Countertops with Integrated Features** — Dental countertops may have custom edge profiles, integral sinks, equipment cutouts.\n10. **18-Page Hardware Spec** — Complex hardware schedule — likely consultant-specified. Budget accordingly.\n\n### 🟢 NOTES\n11. **Sheet Flooring Heat-Welded Seams** — Requires certified installer.\n12. **Blocking/Backing Coordination** — Cross-reference all wall-mounted items (accessories, wall protection, equipment) against framing scope.\n13. **Partition Two-Face Rule** — When counting partitions, account for different finishes on each face (e.g., tile one side, paint other side).\n14. **Demo Separate from Rooms** — Per BluePrint rules, demo quantities are independent of new construction room finishes.\n15. **Access/Height** — Standard 5th floor commercial ceiling heights expected. Flag any double-height or mechanical mezzanine spaces from drawings.\n\n---\n\n## NEXT STEPS\n\n1. **Parse drawing sheets** (Parts 2-7) for:\n   - Demolition plans → verify demo quantities\n   - Floor plans → room-by-room finish schedule\n   - Partition types/schedule → GWB, framing, fire ratings\n   - Door schedule → hardware sets, fire ratings\n   - Reflected ceiling plans → ACT types, GWB ceiling areas\n   - Finish schedule → paint colors, floor types, wall types per room\n   - Details → wall sections, partition details, millwork details\n\n2. **Quantity verification** against bid breakdown for each trade\n\n3. **Cross-reference cut sheets** (end of spec PDF) against bid items for specific product models\n\n---\n\n*Generated by BluePrint — Construction Document Intelligence Engine*  \n*Analysis Date: 2025-01-30*","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1769807688402}}
{"type":"message","id":"118b2174","parentId":"7f74a57a","timestamp":"2026-01-30T21:14:48.426Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017W19ktVPuRyh11REGDEziM","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Takeoff Checklist — HHC South Brooklyn Health Dental Suite 5th Floor\n## Project #26202103 | Cross-Reference of Bid Breakdown vs Drawing Data\n\n**Generated from:** bid_breakdown.json (298 items), room_schedule.json, finish_schedule.json, door_schedule.json, partition_schedule.json, scope_analysis.md  \n**Status:** ⚠️ Many quantities still blank in bid breakdown — this checklist identifies what data we have and what's missing.\n\n---\n\n## LEGEND\n- ✅ = Data available from drawings\n- ⚠️ = Partial data / needs verification\n- ❌ = No data extracted yet — needs manual takeoff\n- 🔴 = Discrepancy or flag\n\n---\n\n## 1. GENERAL CONDITIONS & OVERHEAD (Items 1-7)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | Bonds | LS | N/A — cost item | ✅ |\n| 2 | Insurance | LS | N/A — cost item | ✅ |\n| 3 | Temporary Walkoff Mats | EA | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 4 | Temporary Sticky Mats | EA | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 5 | Dust Control HEPA Filters | LS | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 6 | Project Supervision | MO | N/A — schedule-driven | ✅ |\n| 7 | Hazmat Abatement | LS | 🔴 **UNKNOWN SCOPE** — no abatement survey in drawings. Old hospital = high ACM risk. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 2. EXISTING CONDITIONS / DEMOLITION (Items 8-23)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 8 | Demo Interior Partitions | SF | Demo plan DM-100.00 (part3/p10) available. Need linear footage × height measurement. | ❌ |\n| 9 | Demo Floor Finishes (VCT, adhesive, base, saddles) | SF | Demo plan available. Approximate suite area ~3,500-4,000 SF total. | ⚠️ |\n| 10 | Demo Ceiling Finishes (ACT & GWB) | SF | Demo RCP DM-200.00 (part3/p11) available. | ❌ |\n| 11 | R&R Ceilings Floor Below (10% replace) | SF | 4th floor RCP A-201.00 (part3/p15) available. | ❌ |\n| 12 | Demo Single Doors | EA | Demo plan should show doors to remove. | ❌ |\n| 13 | Demo Millwork | LF | Demo plan should show. | ❌ |\n| 14 | New Door Opening in Masonry Wall inc Lintel | LOC | Construction plan A-100.00 — check for new openings in CMU. | ❌ |\n| 15 | Remove Ceramic Tile on Wall to Remain | SF | Demo plan — look for tile demo areas. | ❌ |\n| 16 | Remove Concrete Pad | SF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 17 | Remove Chair Rail | LF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 18 | Remove Refrigerator | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 19 | Remove Access Doors | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 20 | Remove Wall Mtd Shelving | LF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 21 | Remove Floor Slab Recessed Boxes | SF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 22 | Remove Interior Glazing | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 23 | Carting Fixtures | EA | Sum of all demo items. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 KEY GAP:** Demo plans (part3/pages 10-11) have NOT been quantified. Need manual takeoff from demolition plans for all demo items.\n\n---\n\n## 3. CONCRETE (Item 24)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 24 | Repair/Patch Subflooring | SF | Allowance item — driven by demo conditions. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 4. MASONRY (Item 25)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 25 | New Partition Infill - 6\" | SF | Partition type C00 identified. Count from construction plan A-100.00. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 5. METALS (Items 26-30)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 26 | Ceiling Mounted Equipment Supports | LS | MEP coordination item. | ❌ |\n| 27 | New/Modify Dunnage | LS | Roof plan/structural. | ❌ |\n| 28 | Insulated Metal Panel @ Removed AC Units | EA | Exterior wall condition — check structural/arch. | ❌ |\n| 29 | SS Millwork Base (ALLOW) | LF | Not shown on drawings per bid description. | ⚠️ |\n| 30 | Misc. Metals | LS | Allowance. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 6. WOOD & PLASTICS / MILLWORK (Items 31-39)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 31 | PLAM Base Cabinets | LF | Enlarged plans A-650 thru A-655 show millwork. Finish PL-1 (Formica) and PL-3 (Wilsonart). | ⚠️ |\n| 32 | PLAM Upper Cabinets | LF | Same sheets. | ⚠️ |\n| 33 | PLAM Countertops | LF | Same sheets. Laminate per PL-1/PL-3. | ⚠️ |\n| 34 | Reception Desk | LF | A-602.00 (part3/p19) — reception elevations. | ⚠️ |\n| 35 | Cabinets Behind Reception | EA | A-602.00. | ⚠️ |\n| 36 | Crash Rail | EA | Wall protection details — count from corridor elevations A-601.00. | ❌ |\n| 37 | Acrovyn Wall Panel | SF | Spec references Koroseal/Acrovyn. Count from plans. | ❌ |\n| 38 | Shelving | LF | Enlarged room plans. | ❌ |\n| 39 | Misc. Rough Carpentry | SF | Blocking for accessories, equipment. | ❌ |\n\n**Finish cross-ref:** Cabinets use PL-1 (Formica Matte Wood Brushstroke #06998-58) for base cabinets, PL-3 (Wilsonart Blond Echo 7939-38) for upper and base cabinets.\n\n---\n\n## 7. THERMAL & MOISTURE PROTECTION (Items 40-43)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 40 | Caulk and Sealant | SF | Proportional to partition LF. | ❌ |\n| 41 | Firestopping | SF | Proportional to fire-rated partition penetrations. W2 type = 1-hr rated. | ❌ |\n| 42 | Waterproof Toilet Room Floors | SF | Rooms: Staff Toilet (SN07, ~45 SF), Patient Toilet (SN05, ~45 SF), ADA Restroom (SN0AA, ~49 SF). **Total ~139 SF.** | ✅ |\n| 43 | Roofing Restoration @ New Dunnage | LS | Roof work. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 8. OPENINGS / DOORS (Items 44-49)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 44 | Single Door Non-Rated | EA | ✅ Door schedule: ~22 non-rated single doors (doors 2-8, 10-17, 19-25). **VERIFY exact count.** | ⚠️ |\n| 45 | Single Door Non-Rated w/ Vision Panel | EA | ✅ Door schedule: ~2 doors with vision panels (doors 4 and 18). | ⚠️ |\n| 46 | Single Door Non-Rated w/ Vision Panel & Louver | EA | ⚠️ Could not clearly identify louver doors from image. **VERIFY.** | ❌ |\n| 47 | Double Door with Louver | EA | ⚠️ Likely Mechanical Room. Not clear from schedule. **VERIFY.** | ❌ |\n| 48 | Sliding Pocket Aluminum Door (3'-4.5\" x 6'11.5\") | EA | ⚠️ Door 18 or separate entry. Bid expects specific pocket door. **Count = likely 1.** | ⚠️ |\n| 49 | Access Doors | EA | Not on architectural door schedule — MEP driven. Count from MEP plans. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 FLAG:** Door 1 (Mechanical Room) has 3/4-hr fire rating — but bid items 44-48 all say \"Non-Rated.\" **WHERE IS THE FIRE-RATED DOOR in the bid breakdown?** Either: (a) the mech room door rating was misread, (b) it's included in a non-rated line item as an upgrade, or (c) it's missing from the bid. **MUST CLARIFY.**\n\n---\n\n## 9. FINISHES — WALLS (Items 50-55)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 50 | W32 - 3-5/8\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side, non-rated | SF | Partition type W3 (inferred). Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 51 | W32 - 3-5/8\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side, 1-HR | SF | Partition type W2. **🔴 Drawing shows 2 layers GWB for 1-hr. Bid says 1 layer. DISCREPANCY.** | ❌ |\n| 52 | F21 - 2-1/2\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB one side | SF | Partition type F1 (furring). Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 53 | W62 - 6\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side | SF | Partition type W4. Plumbing walls. Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 54 | Moisture Resistant GWB @ Wall Tile | SF | Restrooms + any tile-backed walls. ~139 SF restroom walls + decon area. | ⚠️ |\n| 55 | Wall Tile | SF | Restrooms per finish schedule. Porcelain per spec 093013. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 CRITICAL FLAG:** Item 51 describes 1-HR rated partition with single layer 5/8\" GWB each side. Standard 1-HR rating (UL U419) requires **2 layers** of 5/8\" Type X GWB each side. Either the bid description is simplified (pricing should reflect 2 layers), or it's a different UL assembly. **MUST CLARIFY before pricing.**\n\n---\n\n## 10. FINISHES — FLOORS (Items 56-61)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 56 | Welded Seam Vinyl Sheet Flooring + Base | SF | Clinical areas — dental rooms, corridors, etc. Flash cove base FCB-1 specified. | ❌ |\n| 57 | Porcelain Floor Tile @ Restroom | SF | Restrooms: ~139 SF (3 restrooms). | ⚠️ |\n| 58 | Epoxy Floor Paint | LF | 🔴 **Unit is LF not SF** — unusual. May be epoxy at transitions or specific areas. | ⚠️ |\n| 59 | Porcelain Tile Wall Base - 6\" High | LF | Restroom perimeters. Estimate ~80 LF for 3 restrooms. | ⚠️ |\n| 60 | Stone Saddle | LF | At every door threshold where flooring changes. ~25 doors × ~3' = ~75 LF. | ⚠️ |\n| 61 | Rubber Base | EA | 🔴 **Unit is EA** — unusual for base. May be per stick/box. WB-1 (Sterling Silver) at lobby, WB-2 (Colonial Gray) at clinical. | ⚠️ |\n\n### Room-to-Finish Cross-Reference (from finish schedule + room schedule):\n\n| Room Type | Floor | Base | Walls | Ceiling |\n|-----------|-------|------|-------|---------|\n| Dental 1-7 (7 rooms, ~120-140 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint PT-1 or PT-2 | ACT washable |\n| Oral Surgery 1-2 (2 rooms, ~153 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Hygienist 1-2 (2 rooms, ~103-106 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Recovery (1 room, ~99 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Dental Lab (~114 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT |\n| Staff/Patient Toilets + ADA (~139 SF total) | Porcelain tile | Porcelain tile base 6\"H | Porcelain wall tile to ht | GWB ceiling |\n| Corridors (~857 SF total) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-2 vinyl base | Paint PT-2 + Acrovyn | ACT |\n| Waiting (~area uncertain) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-1 vinyl base | Paint PT-3 or PT-4 | ACT |\n| Reception (~161 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-1 vinyl base | Paint | ACT |\n| Mechanical Room (~403 SF) | Epoxy paint | None/utility | Paint | Open/GWB |\n| Dental Equipment (~102 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint | ACT |\n| Clean/Decon (~38-68 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint + possible tile | ACT washable |\n| Panorex (~32 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint + **possible lead-lined GWB** | ACT/GWB |\n| Storage (~30 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet or epoxy | WB-2 | Paint | ACT |\n\n**Estimated total areas (rough):**\n- Welded vinyl sheet flooring: ~2,800-3,200 SF (all clinical + corridors)\n- Porcelain floor tile: ~139 SF (restrooms)\n- Epoxy floor paint: ~403 SF (mechanical) — but unit is LF??\n- **⚠️ These are rough estimates from room schedule. Room areas have uncertainty notes. Use for sanity check only.**\n\n---\n\n## 11. FINISHES — CEILINGS (Items 62-64)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 62 | ACT | SF | RCP A-200.00 (part3/p14). Non-clinical areas. | ❌ |\n| 63 | ACT - Washable | SF | Clinical rooms per RCP. Healthcare-grade Armstrong. | ❌ |\n| 64 | Gypsum Ceiling | SF | Restrooms, soffits, mechanical. Per RCP. | ❌ |\n\n**Need:** Takeoff from RCP to split ACT standard vs washable vs GWB ceiling areas.\n\n---\n\n## 12. FINISHES — PAINT (Items 65-67)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 65 | Paint Interior Partitions | SF | All new partitions × 2 faces × wall height. | ❌ |\n| 66 | Paint New Doors and Frames | LVS | ~25 active doors = ~25 leaves. | ⚠️ |\n| 67 | Paint Gyp Ceiling | SF | Same area as item 64. | ❌ |\n\n**Paint colors (Benjamin Moore):**\n- PT-1: Nimbus #1465 (Semi-Gloss) — clinical rooms\n- PT-2: Grey Huron CC-520 (Eggshell) — corridors/support\n- PT-3: Old Blue Jeans #839 (Eggshell) — accent/waiting\n- PT-4: Cloud White OC-130 (Eggshell) — ceilings/trim\n\n---\n\n## 13. SPECIALTIES (Items 68-80)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 68 | New Corner Guards | EA | Count from corridor plan. | ❌ |\n| 69 | Wall Protection | SF | Acrovyn panels in corridors. A-601.00 elevations. | ❌ |\n| 70 | Partition Closure | EA | At partial-height walls. | ❌ |\n| 71 | Grab Bar Set | EA | 3 restrooms × 1 set = **3 EA** (minimum). ADA requires at WC. | ⚠️ |\n| 72 | Soap Dispensers | EA | 3 restrooms + handwash sinks. Estimate **6-10 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 73 | Toilet Tissue/Seat Cover/Waste Unit | EA | 3 restrooms = **3 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 74 | Glass Mirrors w/ SS Frame | EA | 3 restrooms + possible dental. **3-5 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 75 | Towel Dispenser / Waste Receptacle | EA | 3 restrooms = **3 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 76 | Baby Changing Stations | EA | Per enlarged restroom plans A-655.00. Likely **1-2 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 77 | Backpainted Glass | EA | Reception/waiting area. Count from elevations. | ❌ |\n| 78 | Tackboards | EA | Staff areas. Count from plans. | ❌ |\n| 79 | Fire Extinguishers | EA | Per egress plan G-110.00. Count from plan. | ❌ |\n| 80 | Misc. Specialties | LS | Allowance. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 14. FURNISHINGS (Items 81-82)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 81 | Solid Surface Countertops | LF | Corian SS-1 (Glacier White), SS-2 (Silver Gray), SS-3 (Frosty White Mirage). At dental rooms, lab, decon. | ❌ |\n| 82 | Mecho Shade - Manual | SF | At exterior windows. Count from window plan. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 15. FIRE PROTECTION (Items 83-89)\n*Sub trade — quantities from MEP drawings (part4/part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 83-87 | Sprinkler piping and heads | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n| 88-89 | Misc FP | LS | N/A |\n\n---\n\n## 16. PLUMBING (Items 90-135)\n*Sub trade — quantities from plumbing drawings (part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 90-135 | All plumbing items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n**Key counts from room schedule:**\n- Water closets: 3 restrooms = **3 EA** (item 123)\n- Lavatories: 3 restrooms = **3 EA** (item 124)\n- Exam room sinks: ~15+ clinical rooms = **~15 EA** (item 125) — verify\n- Dental chairs to install: 9 dental + 2 oral surg + 2 hygienist = **13 EA** (item 130) — verify\n- Eyewash: **1 EA** minimum (item 126)\n- Water cooler: **1 EA** (item 127)\n\n---\n\n## 17. HVAC (Items 136-195)\n*Sub trade — quantities from mechanical drawings (part4)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 136-195 | All HVAC items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n---\n\n## 18. ELECTRICAL (Items 196-298)\n*Sub trade — quantities from electrical drawings (part4/part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 196-298 | All electrical items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY OF DATA GAPS\n\n### What We Have ✅\n1. **Door schedule** — 25 active doors identified with room assignments, sizes, fire ratings\n2. **Partition types** — W1, W2, W2c, W4, F1, C00 identified with assembly details\n3. **Finish schedule** — Paint colors (BM), laminate types, solid surface, base types, flooring types\n4. **Room schedule** — 30 rooms with approximate areas (many with uncertainty flags)\n5. **Scope analysis** — Category-by-category spec requirements\n6. **Drawing index** — All sheets catalogued\n\n### What's Missing ❌\n1. **All quantity takeoffs** — No actual SF/LF/EA counts from plans\n2. **Demo quantities** — Not measured from demolition plans\n3. **Partition linear footage** — Not measured from construction plan\n4. **Ceiling areas by type** — Not measured from RCP\n5. **Millwork lengths** — Not measured from enlarged plans\n6. **MEP quantities** — Not taken off from MEP drawings\n7. **Exact door sizes** — Size key (A/B/C/D dimensions) not fully legible\n8. **Room finish assignments** — Individual room finish codes not fully extracted from A-400.00\n\n### Critical Discrepancies 🔴\n1. **Item 51 — 1-HR partition GWB layers:** Bid says 1 layer; UL U419 requires 2 layers each side. Price for 2 layers.\n2. **Fire-rated door missing from bid:** Door 1 (Mech Room) = 3/4-HR rated, but no fire-rated door line item in breakdown.\n3. **Item 58 — Epoxy floor in LF units:** Should this be SF? Or is it epoxy at a linear condition (threshold/transition)?\n4. **Item 61 — Rubber base in EA units:** Unusual. Probably per box/carton. Clarify.\n5. **Room areas uncertain:** Many rooms have multiple possible area readings. Use as rough check only.\n6. **Door 9 \"NOT USED\":** Verify this isn't a missed door.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n1. **Priority 1:** Measure partition types/lengths from A-100.00 construction plan\n2. **Priority 2:** Count doors by type on plan to verify schedule\n3. **Priority 3:** Measure ceiling areas by type from RCP A-200.00\n4. **Priority 4:** Measure flooring areas from finish plan A-400.00\n5. **Priority 5:** Quantify demo from DM-100.00 and DM-200.00\n6. **Priority 6:** Measure millwork from enlarged plans A-650 through A-655\n7. **Priority 7:** Issue RFIs for discrepancies noted above\n8. **Priority 8:** MEP subs to take off their own quantities from parts 4-5\n\n---\n\n*Generated for bid preparation — all quantities flagged as estimates must be verified before final pricing.*"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":20,"aggregated":"# Takeoff Checklist — HHC South Brooklyn Health Dental Suite 5th Floor\n## Project #26202103 | Cross-Reference of Bid Breakdown vs Drawing Data\n\n**Generated from:** bid_breakdown.json (298 items), room_schedule.json, finish_schedule.json, door_schedule.json, partition_schedule.json, scope_analysis.md  \n**Status:** ⚠️ Many quantities still blank in bid breakdown — this checklist identifies what data we have and what's missing.\n\n---\n\n## LEGEND\n- ✅ = Data available from drawings\n- ⚠️ = Partial data / needs verification\n- ❌ = No data extracted yet — needs manual takeoff\n- 🔴 = Discrepancy or flag\n\n---\n\n## 1. GENERAL CONDITIONS & OVERHEAD (Items 1-7)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | Bonds | LS | N/A — cost item | ✅ |\n| 2 | Insurance | LS | N/A — cost item | ✅ |\n| 3 | Temporary Walkoff Mats | EA | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 4 | Temporary Sticky Mats | EA | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 5 | Dust Control HEPA Filters | LS | N/A — means & methods | ✅ |\n| 6 | Project Supervision | MO | N/A — schedule-driven | ✅ |\n| 7 | Hazmat Abatement | LS | 🔴 **UNKNOWN SCOPE** — no abatement survey in drawings. Old hospital = high ACM risk. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 2. EXISTING CONDITIONS / DEMOLITION (Items 8-23)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 8 | Demo Interior Partitions | SF | Demo plan DM-100.00 (part3/p10) available. Need linear footage × height measurement. | ❌ |\n| 9 | Demo Floor Finishes (VCT, adhesive, base, saddles) | SF | Demo plan available. Approximate suite area ~3,500-4,000 SF total. | ⚠️ |\n| 10 | Demo Ceiling Finishes (ACT & GWB) | SF | Demo RCP DM-200.00 (part3/p11) available. | ❌ |\n| 11 | R&R Ceilings Floor Below (10% replace) | SF | 4th floor RCP A-201.00 (part3/p15) available. | ❌ |\n| 12 | Demo Single Doors | EA | Demo plan should show doors to remove. | ❌ |\n| 13 | Demo Millwork | LF | Demo plan should show. | ❌ |\n| 14 | New Door Opening in Masonry Wall inc Lintel | LOC | Construction plan A-100.00 — check for new openings in CMU. | ❌ |\n| 15 | Remove Ceramic Tile on Wall to Remain | SF | Demo plan — look for tile demo areas. | ❌ |\n| 16 | Remove Concrete Pad | SF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 17 | Remove Chair Rail | LF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 18 | Remove Refrigerator | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 19 | Remove Access Doors | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 20 | Remove Wall Mtd Shelving | LF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 21 | Remove Floor Slab Recessed Boxes | SF | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 22 | Remove Interior Glazing | EA | Demo plan. | ❌ |\n| 23 | Carting Fixtures | EA | Sum of all demo items. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 KEY GAP:** Demo plans (part3/pages 10-11) have NOT been quantified. Need manual takeoff from demolition plans for all demo items.\n\n---\n\n## 3. CONCRETE (Item 24)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 24 | Repair/Patch Subflooring | SF | Allowance item — driven by demo conditions. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 4. MASONRY (Item 25)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 25 | New Partition Infill - 6\" | SF | Partition type C00 identified. Count from construction plan A-100.00. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 5. METALS (Items 26-30)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 26 | Ceiling Mounted Equipment Supports | LS | MEP coordination item. | ❌ |\n| 27 | New/Modify Dunnage | LS | Roof plan/structural. | ❌ |\n| 28 | Insulated Metal Panel @ Removed AC Units | EA | Exterior wall condition — check structural/arch. | ❌ |\n| 29 | SS Millwork Base (ALLOW) | LF | Not shown on drawings per bid description. | ⚠️ |\n| 30 | Misc. Metals | LS | Allowance. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 6. WOOD & PLASTICS / MILLWORK (Items 31-39)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 31 | PLAM Base Cabinets | LF | Enlarged plans A-650 thru A-655 show millwork. Finish PL-1 (Formica) and PL-3 (Wilsonart). | ⚠️ |\n| 32 | PLAM Upper Cabinets | LF | Same sheets. | ⚠️ |\n| 33 | PLAM Countertops | LF | Same sheets. Laminate per PL-1/PL-3. | ⚠️ |\n| 34 | Reception Desk | LF | A-602.00 (part3/p19) — reception elevations. | ⚠️ |\n| 35 | Cabinets Behind Reception | EA | A-602.00. | ⚠️ |\n| 36 | Crash Rail | EA | Wall protection details — count from corridor elevations A-601.00. | ❌ |\n| 37 | Acrovyn Wall Panel | SF | Spec references Koroseal/Acrovyn. Count from plans. | ❌ |\n| 38 | Shelving | LF | Enlarged room plans. | ❌ |\n| 39 | Misc. Rough Carpentry | SF | Blocking for accessories, equipment. | ❌ |\n\n**Finish cross-ref:** Cabinets use PL-1 (Formica Matte Wood Brushstroke #06998-58) for base cabinets, PL-3 (Wilsonart Blond Echo 7939-38) for upper and base cabinets.\n\n---\n\n## 7. THERMAL & MOISTURE PROTECTION (Items 40-43)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 40 | Caulk and Sealant | SF | Proportional to partition LF. | ❌ |\n| 41 | Firestopping | SF | Proportional to fire-rated partition penetrations. W2 type = 1-hr rated. | ❌ |\n| 42 | Waterproof Toilet Room Floors | SF | Rooms: Staff Toilet (SN07, ~45 SF), Patient Toilet (SN05, ~45 SF), ADA Restroom (SN0AA, ~49 SF). **Total ~139 SF.** | ✅ |\n| 43 | Roofing Restoration @ New Dunnage | LS | Roof work. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 8. OPENINGS / DOORS (Items 44-49)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 44 | Single Door Non-Rated | EA | ✅ Door schedule: ~22 non-rated single doors (doors 2-8, 10-17, 19-25). **VERIFY exact count.** | ⚠️ |\n| 45 | Single Door Non-Rated w/ Vision Panel | EA | ✅ Door schedule: ~2 doors with vision panels (doors 4 and 18). | ⚠️ |\n| 46 | Single Door Non-Rated w/ Vision Panel & Louver | EA | ⚠️ Could not clearly identify louver doors from image. **VERIFY.** | ❌ |\n| 47 | Double Door with Louver | EA | ⚠️ Likely Mechanical Room. Not clear from schedule. **VERIFY.** | ❌ |\n| 48 | Sliding Pocket Aluminum Door (3'-4.5\" x 6'11.5\") | EA | ⚠️ Door 18 or separate entry. Bid expects specific pocket door. **Count = likely 1.** | ⚠️ |\n| 49 | Access Doors | EA | Not on architectural door schedule — MEP driven. Count from MEP plans. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 FLAG:** Door 1 (Mechanical Room) has 3/4-hr fire rating — but bid items 44-48 all say \"Non-Rated.\" **WHERE IS THE FIRE-RATED DOOR in the bid breakdown?** Either: (a) the mech room door rating was misread, (b) it's included in a non-rated line item as an upgrade, or (c) it's missing from the bid. **MUST CLARIFY.**\n\n---\n\n## 9. FINISHES — WALLS (Items 50-55)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 50 | W32 - 3-5/8\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side, non-rated | SF | Partition type W3 (inferred). Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 51 | W32 - 3-5/8\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side, 1-HR | SF | Partition type W2. **🔴 Drawing shows 2 layers GWB for 1-hr. Bid says 1 layer. DISCREPANCY.** | ❌ |\n| 52 | F21 - 2-1/2\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB one side | SF | Partition type F1 (furring). Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 53 | W62 - 6\" studs, 1× 5/8\" GWB ea side | SF | Partition type W4. Plumbing walls. Measure from A-100.00. | ❌ |\n| 54 | Moisture Resistant GWB @ Wall Tile | SF | Restrooms + any tile-backed walls. ~139 SF restroom walls + decon area. | ⚠️ |\n| 55 | Wall Tile | SF | Restrooms per finish schedule. Porcelain per spec 093013. | ❌ |\n\n**🔴 CRITICAL FLAG:** Item 51 describes 1-HR rated partition with single layer 5/8\" GWB each side. Standard 1-HR rating (UL U419) requires **2 layers** of 5/8\" Type X GWB each side. Either the bid description is simplified (pricing should reflect 2 layers), or it's a different UL assembly. **MUST CLARIFY before pricing.**\n\n---\n\n## 10. FINISHES — FLOORS (Items 56-61)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 56 | Welded Seam Vinyl Sheet Flooring + Base | SF | Clinical areas — dental rooms, corridors, etc. Flash cove base FCB-1 specified. | ❌ |\n| 57 | Porcelain Floor Tile @ Restroom | SF | Restrooms: ~139 SF (3 restrooms). | ⚠️ |\n| 58 | Epoxy Floor Paint | LF | 🔴 **Unit is LF not SF** — unusual. May be epoxy at transitions or specific areas. | ⚠️ |\n| 59 | Porcelain Tile Wall Base - 6\" High | LF | Restroom perimeters. Estimate ~80 LF for 3 restrooms. | ⚠️ |\n| 60 | Stone Saddle | LF | At every door threshold where flooring changes. ~25 doors × ~3' = ~75 LF. | ⚠️ |\n| 61 | Rubber Base | EA | 🔴 **Unit is EA** — unusual for base. May be per stick/box. WB-1 (Sterling Silver) at lobby, WB-2 (Colonial Gray) at clinical. | ⚠️ |\n\n### Room-to-Finish Cross-Reference (from finish schedule + room schedule):\n\n| Room Type | Floor | Base | Walls | Ceiling |\n|-----------|-------|------|-------|---------|\n| Dental 1-7 (7 rooms, ~120-140 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint PT-1 or PT-2 | ACT washable |\n| Oral Surgery 1-2 (2 rooms, ~153 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Hygienist 1-2 (2 rooms, ~103-106 SF ea) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Recovery (1 room, ~99 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT washable |\n| Dental Lab (~114 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 flash cove | Paint | ACT |\n| Staff/Patient Toilets + ADA (~139 SF total) | Porcelain tile | Porcelain tile base 6\"H | Porcelain wall tile to ht | GWB ceiling |\n| Corridors (~857 SF total) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-2 vinyl base | Paint PT-2 + Acrovyn | ACT |\n| Waiting (~area uncertain) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-1 vinyl base | Paint PT-3 or PT-4 | ACT |\n| Reception (~161 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | WB-1 vinyl base | Paint | ACT |\n| Mechanical Room (~403 SF) | Epoxy paint | None/utility | Paint | Open/GWB |\n| Dental Equipment (~102 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint | ACT |\n| Clean/Decon (~38-68 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint + possible tile | ACT washable |\n| Panorex (~32 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet | FCB-1 | Paint + **possible lead-lined GWB** | ACT/GWB |\n| Storage (~30 SF) | Welded vinyl sheet or epoxy | WB-2 | Paint | ACT |\n\n**Estimated total areas (rough):**\n- Welded vinyl sheet flooring: ~2,800-3,200 SF (all clinical + corridors)\n- Porcelain floor tile: ~139 SF (restrooms)\n- Epoxy floor paint: ~403 SF (mechanical) — but unit is LF??\n- **⚠️ These are rough estimates from room schedule. Room areas have uncertainty notes. Use for sanity check only.**\n\n---\n\n## 11. FINISHES — CEILINGS (Items 62-64)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 62 | ACT | SF | RCP A-200.00 (part3/p14). Non-clinical areas. | ❌ |\n| 63 | ACT - Washable | SF | Clinical rooms per RCP. Healthcare-grade Armstrong. | ❌ |\n| 64 | Gypsum Ceiling | SF | Restrooms, soffits, mechanical. Per RCP. | ❌ |\n\n**Need:** Takeoff from RCP to split ACT standard vs washable vs GWB ceiling areas.\n\n---\n\n## 12. FINISHES — PAINT (Items 65-67)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 65 | Paint Interior Partitions | SF | All new partitions × 2 faces × wall height. | ❌ |\n| 66 | Paint New Doors and Frames | LVS | ~25 active doors = ~25 leaves. | ⚠️ |\n| 67 | Paint Gyp Ceiling | SF | Same area as item 64. | ❌ |\n\n**Paint colors (Benjamin Moore):**\n- PT-1: Nimbus #1465 (Semi-Gloss) — clinical rooms\n- PT-2: Grey Huron CC-520 (Eggshell) — corridors/support\n- PT-3: Old Blue Jeans #839 (Eggshell) — accent/waiting\n- PT-4: Cloud White OC-130 (Eggshell) — ceilings/trim\n\n---\n\n## 13. SPECIALTIES (Items 68-80)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 68 | New Corner Guards | EA | Count from corridor plan. | ❌ |\n| 69 | Wall Protection | SF | Acrovyn panels in corridors. A-601.00 elevations. | ❌ |\n| 70 | Partition Closure | EA | At partial-height walls. | ❌ |\n| 71 | Grab Bar Set | EA | 3 restrooms × 1 set = **3 EA** (minimum). ADA requires at WC. | ⚠️ |\n| 72 | Soap Dispensers | EA | 3 restrooms + handwash sinks. Estimate **6-10 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 73 | Toilet Tissue/Seat Cover/Waste Unit | EA | 3 restrooms = **3 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 74 | Glass Mirrors w/ SS Frame | EA | 3 restrooms + possible dental. **3-5 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 75 | Towel Dispenser / Waste Receptacle | EA | 3 restrooms = **3 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 76 | Baby Changing Stations | EA | Per enlarged restroom plans A-655.00. Likely **1-2 EA.** | ⚠️ |\n| 77 | Backpainted Glass | EA | Reception/waiting area. Count from elevations. | ❌ |\n| 78 | Tackboards | EA | Staff areas. Count from plans. | ❌ |\n| 79 | Fire Extinguishers | EA | Per egress plan G-110.00. Count from plan. | ❌ |\n| 80 | Misc. Specialties | LS | Allowance. | ⚠️ |\n\n---\n\n## 14. FURNISHINGS (Items 81-82)\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Drawing Data | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|-------------|--------|\n| 81 | Solid Surface Countertops | LF | Corian SS-1 (Glacier White), SS-2 (Silver Gray), SS-3 (Frosty White Mirage). At dental rooms, lab, decon. | ❌ |\n| 82 | Mecho Shade - Manual | SF | At exterior windows. Count from window plan. | ❌ |\n\n---\n\n## 15. FIRE PROTECTION (Items 83-89)\n*Sub trade — quantities from MEP drawings (part4/part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 83-87 | Sprinkler piping and heads | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n| 88-89 | Misc FP | LS | N/A |\n\n---\n\n## 16. PLUMBING (Items 90-135)\n*Sub trade — quantities from plumbing drawings (part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 90-135 | All plumbing items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n**Key counts from room schedule:**\n- Water closets: 3 restrooms = **3 EA** (item 123)\n- Lavatories: 3 restrooms = **3 EA** (item 124)\n- Exam room sinks: ~15+ clinical rooms = **~15 EA** (item 125) — verify\n- Dental chairs to install: 9 dental + 2 oral surg + 2 hygienist = **13 EA** (item 130) — verify\n- Eyewash: **1 EA** minimum (item 126)\n- Water cooler: **1 EA** (item 127)\n\n---\n\n## 17. HVAC (Items 136-195)\n*Sub trade — quantities from mechanical drawings (part4)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 136-195 | All HVAC items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n---\n\n## 18. ELECTRICAL (Items 196-298)\n*Sub trade — quantities from electrical drawings (part4/part5)*\n\n| Item | Description | Unit | Status |\n|------|-------------|------|--------|\n| 196-298 | All electrical items | Various | ❌ MEP takeoff needed |\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY OF DATA GAPS\n\n### What We Have ✅\n1. **Door schedule** — 25 active doors identified with room assignments, sizes, fire ratings\n2. **Partition types** — W1, W2, W2c, W4, F1, C00 identified with assembly details\n3. **Finish schedule** — Paint colors (BM), laminate types, solid surface, base types, flooring types\n4. **Room schedule** — 30 rooms with approximate areas (many with uncertainty flags)\n5. **Scope analysis** — Category-by-category spec requirements\n6. **Drawing index** — All sheets catalogued\n\n### What's Missing ❌\n1. **All quantity takeoffs** — No actual SF/LF/EA counts from plans\n2. **Demo quantities** — Not measured from demolition plans\n3. **Partition linear footage** — Not measured from construction plan\n4. **Ceiling areas by type** — Not measured from RCP\n5. **Millwork lengths** — Not measured from enlarged plans\n6. **MEP quantities** — Not taken off from MEP drawings\n7. **Exact door sizes** — Size key (A/B/C/D dimensions) not fully legible\n8. **Room finish assignments** — Individual room finish codes not fully extracted from A-400.00\n\n### Critical Discrepancies 🔴\n1. **Item 51 — 1-HR partition GWB layers:** Bid says 1 layer; UL U419 requires 2 layers each side. Price for 2 layers.\n2. **Fire-rated door missing from bid:** Door 1 (Mech Room) = 3/4-HR rated, but no fire-rated door line item in breakdown.\n3. **Item 58 — Epoxy floor in LF units:** Should this be SF? Or is it epoxy at a linear condition (threshold/transition)?\n4. **Item 61 — Rubber base in EA units:** Unusual. Probably per box/carton. Clarify.\n5. **Room areas uncertain:** Many rooms have multiple possible area readings. Use as rough check only.\n6. **Door 9 \"NOT USED\":** Verify this isn't a missed door.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n1. **Priority 1:** Measure partition types/lengths from A-100.00 construction plan\n2. **Priority 2:** Count doors by type on plan to verify schedule\n3. **Priority 3:** Measure ceiling areas by type from RCP A-200.00\n4. **Priority 4:** Measure flooring areas from finish plan A-400.00\n5. **Priority 5:** Quantify demo from DM-100.00 and DM-200.00\n6. **Priority 6:** Measure millwork from enlarged plans A-650 through A-655\n7. **Priority 7:** Issue RFIs for discrepancies noted above\n8. **Priority 8:** MEP subs to take off their own quantities from parts 4-5\n\n---\n\n*Generated for bid preparation — all quantities flagged as estimates must be verified before final pricing.*","cwd":"/home/ec2-user/clawd"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1769807688423}}
